      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hum, careful, __guest_requet_page_transition() is capping the number of pages to avoid getting stuck too long in the hypervisor. So it is possible for the guest to call a number a bit too big here but nonetheless valid. It will e.g. stop if the physical addresses are not contiguous.\n\nAnd actually speaking of contiguous physical memory... how is it handled? This memory is faulted into the guest. There is no guarantee it will be contiguous. I am afraid the only way here is the private range... which isn\u0027t the most dynamic resource thing we have :-(",
